TEST 38413 -- deny/permit statements for standard IPv6 access list
===========================================================================
Run:    2026-09-24 (device clock 2026-09-23 ~21:40 UTC), tb470
Build:  awplus_main-20260923-20 (re-run: the 2026-09-22 run was on 20260913-1734)
DUT:    IE520 3-member VCStack "IE520-stk" (members 1/3/4)
Path:   tb470 eth3 -> DUT port3.0.9 (ingress, where the ACL would go) -> DUT port3.0.13
        -> tb470 eth1. eth2 (behind IE520-sa via sa3) also captured, to catch leakage.
        A frame counted on eth1 has TRANSITED the DUT.

VERDICT: UNSUPPORTED -- a standard IPv6 access-list cannot be applied to any port on
         this platform (the CLI refuses it), on the new build as on the old.

STEP 0 -- baseline, no ACL (dst 2001:db8:ff::1, UDP, 10 frames each)
      source              role in the planned list       eth1    eth2
      2001:db8:1::1       permit 2001:db8:1::/64          10/10   0
      2001:db8:1::ffff    permit, far end of the /64      10/10   0
      2001:db8:2::1       deny 2001:db8:2::/64            10/10   0
      2001:db8:9::1       matches nothing (implicit deny) 10/10   0

BUILD -- the list is created and stored in order
      IE520-stk(config)# ipv6 access-list standard v6std permit 2001:db8:1::/64
      IE520-stk(config)# ipv6 access-list standard v6std deny 2001:db8:2::/64
      IE520-stk# show ipv6 access-list
      Named Standard IPv6 access list v6std
          4 permit 2001:db8:1::/64
          8 deny   2001:db8:2::/64

APPLY -- refused
      IE520-stk(config)# interface port3.0.9
      IE520-stk(config-if)# ipv6 traffic-filter v6std
      % Access-list does not exist
      show running-config interface port3.0.9 -> no traffic-filter line

  `ipv6 traffic-filter` resolves hardware IPv6 lists only, so a standard list is
  invisible to it (and the error text is misleading: the list does exist). With no
  application point, steps 1-5 (permit, deny, implicit deny, prefix match, first match)
  cannot be driven by traffic. Those semantics are exercised on a hardware IPv6 list in
  AWPTCM-T929. If the case intends a standard list to be port-applicable on the IE520,
  that is the discrepancy to raise.

Cleanup: `no ipv6 access-list standard v6std`; `show ipv6 access-list` empty.
